# The Google tag (gtag.js, Google Ads AW-18386624012) needs googletagmanager in
# script-src plus doubleclick/google-analytics in img-src + connect-src for its
# conversion beacons. It is deliberately NOT given 'unsafe-inline': Google's
# copy-paste snippet puts config in an inline <script>, which we serve from
# js/gtag-init.js instead so this policy stays strict for every other script.
# *.doubleclick.net is wildcarded because the observed beacon (ad.doubleclick.net)
# is only the first hop; later hops use googleads.g.doubleclick.net.
# NOTE: remarketing audiences also beacon country domains (google.co.uk, .de …)
# which CSP cannot wildcard in the TLD position — add them here if that's enabled.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.googleadservices.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googleadservices.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com; connect-src https://api.github.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com; frame-src 'self' https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.googletagmanager.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none';

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# 1 day, not 7: a Pages deploy does NOT purge the edge cache, so a long TTL
# means a replaced card keeps being served. Bump the ?v= in the og:image
# meta tags for an immediate swap.
/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Lemon Squeezy's checkout overlay (lemon.js) needs its own script/frame/connect
# allowances — scoped to just this page so the rest of the site keeps the
# strict default CSP above untouched. Wildcarded to *.lemonsqueezy.com since
# their own docs and the actual embed snippet disagree on the exact subdomain
# (app.lemonsqueezy.com vs assets.lemonsqueezy.com).
#
# `! Content-Security-Policy` IS LOAD-BEARING — do not remove it.
# Cloudflare Pages APPENDS a specific rule's headers to those from a broader
# rule; it does not replace them. Without the unset, /purchase was served TWO
# CSP headers (the /* one and this one), and browsers enforce the INTERSECTION
# of every CSP header — so *.lemonsqueezy.com, absent from /*, stayed blocked
# and lemon.js never executed (the checkout overlay silently degraded to a
# plain redirect). Net rule: per-path blocks here can only ADD restrictions;
# relaxing one path REQUIRES unsetting the inherited header first.
# Verified on a real Pages preview deploy: with the unset, /purchase gets
# exactly 1 CSP header and createLemonSqueezy is defined, while / still gets 1
# and still excludes lemonsqueezy. A local static server does NOT reproduce
# this (it sends only the most specific header) — test header changes on a
# preview deployment, not localhost.
/purchase
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.googleadservices.com https://*.lemonsqueezy.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googleadservices.com https://*.lemonsqueezy.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com; connect-src https://api.github.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://*.lemonsqueezy.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com; frame-src https://*.lemonsqueezy.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.googletagmanager.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none';

